<title>UK: Commerzbank unit sets NZ$100 mln four-year bond.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank unit sets NZ$100 mln four-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Hambros Bank and Commerzbank.  BORROWER   COMMERZBANK OVERSEAS FINANCE</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  COMMERZBANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    NZ$100 MLN    COUPON     6.75 PCT  MATURITY    13.AUG.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.75    PAY DATE   L12.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.75	REOFFER    =	   L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>+=</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/NZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  0.125</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
